<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for Blygger (Developer ID, not sandboxed).

  Intentionally empty: the app needs no hardened-runtime exceptions.
  - Network (blyg API, AI providers, the localhost OAuth callback): the
    hardened runtime doesn't restrict sockets. com.apple.security.network.*
    only matter under the App Sandbox, which this build doesn't enable.
  - Keychain (owner token, API keys via the `keyring` crate): the app's own
    generic-password items in the login keychain need no entitlement.
    keychain-access-groups is only for sharing items or the data-protection
    keychain, which we don't use.
  - Global hotkey (global-hotkey crate): Carbon RegisterEventHotKey, no
    entitlement and no Accessibility permission. (Its CGEventTap path is for
    media keys only, which the app doesn't register.)
  - GPUI/Metal: shaders are compiled by Metal, not JIT'd by us, so no
    cs.allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory.
  - Spawning `claude` / `codex` for the local AI bridges: exec'ing other
    signed binaries needs nothing; they run under their own signatures.
  Add an exception here only with a comment saying what needs it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
